### Describe the bug

The DataListener callback on a bound struct is not called if the value of one of the struct fields is changed or the value of the entire struct is changed. Specifically, if you bind a struct, set up a data listener on the struct, change one of the struct field values, and then call Reload(), the callback on the struct's data listener is not invoked. 

On a related note, a data listener bound to a field of the struct is always called when a value is assigned - even if the new value is the same as the original one. This seems inconsistent with a "notify of change" philosophy.

### How to reproduce

1. Bind a struct
2. Create a DataListener and add it to the struct. Instrument the listener so that you can tell whether the callback has been invoked.
3. Change one of the the field values of the struct
4. Call Reload() on the binding
5. Check the instrumentation on the data listener to verify that the callback was never invoked.

